{
  "raw": {
    "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=48&rid=38479": {
      "title": "Career Center",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Assistant Professor 9 Mo Working Title Assistant Professor 9 Mo - Engineering and Physics Position # F00076 Department Engineering and Physics - HSU Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Faculty # of openings: 1 Location: Henderson State University Proposed Salary Range: $65,000-$75,000.00 Closing: Please note: All postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the closing date.  This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: The Caver College of Aviation, Science, and Nursing at Henderson State University invites applicants for a tenure track position in Mechanical Engineering at the rank of assistant professor to begin January 2027. Henderson State University is located in Arkadelphia, Arkansas, a charming, family-centered community of 11,000 residents situated one hour south of Little Rock, Arkansas on Interstate 30. Nestled in the foothills of the Ouachita Mountains, the community is home to two universities, a strong public school system, a thriving medical community, two recreational rivers, the iconic Lake DeGray, and is approximately 30 miles from historic Hot Springs National Park, one of the great American treasures. Please visit www.hsu.edu, www.arkadelphiaalliance.com or www.arkadelphiaschools.org for more information about Henderson State University and our community. Duties & Responsibilities: Teaching engineering and physics courses at all undergraduate levels Student mentoring Curriculum development and assessment in support of accreditation Senior project supervision Community industry engagement University service. Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: General Days/Hours: Monday-Friday 8am-5pm. Additional Hours as requested and/or needed Other: Applications must include: (1) a cover letter highlighting your particular qualifications for this position; (2) a curriculum vitae; (3) a statement of teaching philosophy; (4) a statement of research interests/achievements; (5) names and contact information for three references; (6) copies of transcripts; Submit all items, in the order stated, as a single PDF file. Review of applications will begin once the position closes and continue until the position is filled. The final applicant for this position will be required to submit to a background screening including a criminal background check pursuant to university policy. The applicant will also be required to provide official transcripts to the Office of the Provost. Under the provisions of the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act, applications are subject to public inspection upon request. Henderson State University is an equal employment opportunity employer committed to excellence. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, national origin, age, protected veteran or disabled status, or genetic information. Minimum Qualifications: Candidates should possess a PhD in mechanical engineering, or a related field at time of the appointment. Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States by the proposed start date. The University will not sponsor a visa for this position. E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Share Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=48&rid=39142": {
      "title": "Career Center",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Assistant Professor 9 Mo Working Title Assistant Professor of Operations Management Position # F00055 Department College of Business - HSU Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Faculty # of openings: 1 Location: Henderson State University Proposed Salary Range: $90,000.00-$96,400.00 Closing: Please note: All postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the closing date.  This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: The College of Business (CoB) at Henderson State University invites applicants for an Assistant Professor of Operations Management. Henderson’s Business program was initially accredited by AACSB in 1998. The position reports to the Dean of CoB. This position will contribute to Henderson’s mission by teaching operations management and related courses, supporting the development of an AI Certificate program, and engaging students in experiential learning opportunities that prepare them for leadership in an evolving business world. Duties & Responsibilities: Develop and teach undergraduate and graduate courses in Operations Management, Supply Chain, Logistics, and related areas. Contribute to the design and launch of a new AI-focused certificate, collaborating with faculty across disciplines to integrate AI into business education. Assess and evaluate instruction. Provide academic and career advisement, recruitment, and retention support for students. Facilitate student learning and help students achieve academic success and retention. Engage in scholarly and/or applied research in operations, supply chain, or AI-related business applications. Monitor and continuously improve instruction to ensure student learning outcomes are met at the course, program, and college level. Connect with local business and industry to strengthen partnerships and experiential learning opportunities. Participate in college and university committees. Attend and participate in faculty meetings, commencement ceremonies, and other required events. Engage in professional development in emerging instructional approaches and AI-related applications in business. Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: • Demonstrated ability or potential to teach operations management and related courses across multiple modalities (traditional, hybrid, online). • Interest in developing and teaching in an AI-related curriculum. • Strong interpersonal, communication, and organizational skills. • Ability to work collaboratively with students, faculty, and industry partners. • Commitment to AACSB standards of teaching, research, and service. • Civility in all interactions. General Days/Hours: Other: Salary & Benefits: Salary and rank will be competitive with AACSB-accredited small schools and commensurate with experience and qualifications. • Medical – university pays the majority of premium • Basic Life Insurance – university pays the premium • Long-term Disability – university pays the majority of premium • Retirement – university matches 6% of salary • Tuition Remission – 75% discount on undergraduate tuition for most programs in the Arkansas State University System; 50% discount on some graduate programs Application Process: Applicants should provide: 1. A cover letter highlighting your particular qualifications for this position. 2. A curriculum vitae. 3. Names and contact information for three professional references. 4. Copies of transcripts. All items should be submitted as a single PDF file in the above order. Review of applications will begin on August 17, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. The position begins August 16, 2027. The final applicant will be required to submit to a background screening, including a criminal background check, pursuant to university policy, and to provide official transcripts to Human Resources. Under the provisions of the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act, applications are subject to public inspection upon request. Minimum Qualifications: • An earned doctorate in Operations Management, Supply Chain, Logistics, Business Analytics, or a closely related area from an AACSB-accredited school is required for appointment as Assistant Professor. ABD candidates nearing completion of his/her dissertation will be considered. Preferred Qualifications: • Evidence of teaching excellence in operations, supply chain, logistics, or analytics. • Experience or interest in AI applications in business or curriculum development. • Refereed publications or demonstrated research potential in operations or AI-related fields. • Professional business/industry experience. E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Share Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=48&rid=39418": {
      "title": "Career Center",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Assistant Professor 9 Mo Working Title Nursing Simulation Coordinator Position # F00148 Department Nursing - HSU Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Faculty # of openings: 1 Location: Henderson State University Proposed Salary Range: $55,000.00 - $62,000.00 Closing: Please note: All postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the closing date.  This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: The Nursing Simulation Coordinator faculty member is responsible for the planning, implementation, evaluation, and continuous quality improvement of simulation-based learning experiences for the BSN program. This position ensures that all simulation activities align with the INACSL Standards of Best Practice: Simulation©, with a strong focus on promoting clinical judgment, patient safety, and professional competency development in pre-licensure nursing students. The coordinator serves as a subject matter expert in simulation pedagogy and collaborates closely with faculty, staff, and administration to enhance student learning outcomes through high-fidelity simulation, task trainers, and hybrid simulation experiences. Duties & Responsibilities: Simulation Development & Implementation Design, implement, and evaluate simulation experiences that reflect course and program learning outcomes across all levels of the curriculum. Ensure simulation activities incorporate INACSL standards for: Simulation Design Outcomes & Objectives Facilitation Pre-briefing & Debriefing Professional Integrity Simulation-Enhanced Interprofessional Education (as applicable) Evaluation Create a psychologically safe learning environment that promotes student engagement and reflective practice. Develop and maintain a library of standardized scenarios, including associated documentation, assessment rubrics, and debriefing guides. Simulation Center Management Oversee the scheduling, preparation, and delivery of simulation experiences, including clinical skill labs and high-fidelity simulations. Maintain and inventory simulation equipment and supplies; coordinate maintenance and repairs with vendors. Operate and troubleshoot simulation technology, including manikins, task trainers, AV systems, and simulation management software. Faculty Support & Collaboration Serve as a resource and coach for all faculty in simulation design and facilitation, helping integrate simulation across courses. Provide faculty development on best practices in simulation education, including effective debriefing models (e.g., DML, PEARLS). Collaborate with course coordinators to align simulation content with didactic and clinical instruction and desired student outcomes. In addition to pre-licensure simulation duties, collaborate as needed with all nursing programs such as Family Nurse Practitioner or RN- BSN for skills practice and check-offs. Actively participates in Department of Nursing faculty meetings and on select departmental, College and University committees Student Learning & Evaluation Facilitate formative and summative simulation experiences to assess clinical reasoning, communication, and safe nursing practice. Ensure appropriate use of validated assessment tools and methods consistent with INACSL's Evaluation standard. Provide feedback to students that is timely, constructive, and aligned with learning objectives. Provide student advisement, holds weekly office hours and counsel student advisees as needed Program Improvement & Innovation Lead continuous quality improvement (CQI) efforts for the simulation program by analyzing data and student performance outcomes. Conduct needs assessments and use outcome data to inform changes in simulation design and delivery. Participate in simulation-related scholarship, research, and/or presentations at professional conferences. Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: CORE COMPETENCIES Quality: Accuracy. Supports improvement and innovation in the workplace. Demonstrates awareness of and supports Nursing Department and HSU operating goals through participation in quality improvement and departmental activities. Uses feedback to improve performance. Job Knowledge: Skills. Demonstrates ability to learn. Keeps abreast of developments in their clinical nursing field, educational pedagogy, and instructional technologies. Understands how job relates to others, relationship of Nursing Department to University committees. Uses resources efficiently. Problem Solving: Teamwork. Takes initiative to identify and solve problems. Identifies problems in a timely manner. Analyzes information and develops alternative solutions. Resolves problems early and works well in groups. Communication: Establishes and maintains open communications to enhance team effort. Presents a personal and positive model of the Nursing Department and HSU students, visitors, fellow faculty and staff and the general public. Verbal and writing ability. Good listening. Keeps others informed. Initiative: Makes continuous effort to identify opportunities to meet/exceed customer needs and expectations. Seeks increased responsibilities. Volunteers readily. Takes individual actions and calculated risks. Asks for help when needed. Adaptability: Demonstrates flexibility in response to unexpected changes in work volume, emergencies, staffing, scheduling, and student needs. Accepts criticism and feedback. Manages competing demands. Changes approach or method to best fit situation. Judgment: Makes decisions in timely manner. Exhibits sound, accurate judgment. Supports and explains reasons for decisions. Follows due process in student assessments and grading. Cost Consciousness: Promotes cost effectiveness through the proper use and conservation of supplies and equipment. Identifies cost saving measures. Cooperation: Establishes effective relationships within the Nursing Department, Henderson State University, and the surround healthcare community. Looks for opportunities to assist co-workers. Works collaboratively with all HSU departments. Exhibits positive outlook and pleasant manner. Resolves conflicts. Dependability: Fulfills work schedule and commitments. Follows instructions. Takes responsibility for own actions. Commits to doing best job possible. Keeps students and supervisors advised of class changes. Safety: Works in a safe manner. Maintains a safe and clean work environment. Reports needed repairs or potential hazards to the appropriate department as soon as identified. Reports all on-the-job injuries and seeks medical attention as appropriate. Role models universal precautions in clinical settings. Confidentiality: Holds in trust the confidences of another. Exhibits behaviors which protect the privacy of HSU students and employees. Exhibits knowledge and compliance with HIPPA when dealing with clinical issues. Corporate Compliance: Maintains awareness of, develops an understanding of, and adheres to all HSU and clinical site compliance program procedures. Is familiar with departmental, academic and university policies and procedures; uses web-site and handbook to assure compliance with policies and procedures. QUALIFICATIONS To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily. The requirements listed below are representative of the knowledge, skill and/or ability required. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals to perform the essential functions. EDUCATION and/or EXPERIENCE Master’s degree in Nursing, current Arkansas registered nurse license, and two years nursing experience are required. Previous teaching experience is preferred. LANGUAGE SKILLS Ability to read, analyze and interpret general business periodicals, professional journals, technical procedures or governmental regulations. Ability to write reports, business correspondence and procedure manuals. Ability to effectively present information and respond to questions from students, faculty, staff and the general public. MATHEMATICAL SKILLS Ability to add, subtract, multiply and divide in all units of measure, using whole numbers, common fractions and decimals. Ability to compute rate, ratio and percent and to draw and interpret bar graphs. Understanding of and ability to compute basic statistical procedures. REASONING ABILITY Ability to interpret complex instructions. Ability to deal with abstract problems involving multiple variable and make decisions under conditions of ambiguity. PHYSICAL DEMANDS The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodation may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. While performing the duties of this job, the employee is regularly required to use hands to finger, handle or feel and talk or hear. The employee frequently is required to sit. The employee is often required to stand, walk, reach with hands and arms, climb or balance and smell. The employee must occasionally life and/or move up to 50 pounds. Specific vision abilities required by this job include close vision, color vision and ability to adjust focus. WORK ENVIRONMENT The work environment characteristics described here are representative of those an employee encounters while performing the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. While performing the duties of this job, the employee is occasionally exposed to moving mechanical parts, outside weather conditions, and risk of electrical shock. The noise level in the work environment is usually quiet. General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Additional hours as requested and/or needed Other: Work Environment: • Primarily based in the university simulation center/lab environment. • Primarily works Monday through Friday during business hours • Occasional off-hours work may be required for simulation events, recruiting events or faculty support. • Moderate physical activity including lifting equipment, preparing lab setups, and standing during simulation sessions. Minimum Qualifications: • Master’s degree in Nursing or Nursing Education (or in progress, within one semester of completion). • Current, unrestricted RN license. • Minimum of 2 years of clinical experience as a registered nurse. • At least 1 year of experience in simulation-based teaching or clinical skills instruction in a nursing education setting. • Demonstrated knowledge of the INACSL Standards of Best Practice: Simulation©. Preferred Qualifications: • Certification as a Healthcare Simulation Educator (CHSE) or Operations Specialist (CHSOS). • Experience teaching or coordinating in an undergraduate nursing education program. • Familiarity with simulation technologies (e.g., Laerdal, CAE, Gaumard), learning management systems, and audiovisual platforms. • Experience using simulation management software (e.g., SimCapture, EMS). E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Share Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=48&rid=39419": {
      "title": "Career Center",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Assistant Professor 9 Mo Working Title Assistant Professor 9 Mo - Nursing Position # F00107 Department Nursing - HSU Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Faculty # of openings: 1 Location: Henderson State University Proposed Salary Range: $55,000.00 - $62,000.00 Closing: Please note: All postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the closing date.  This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: A nursing faculty member will be responsible for curriculum, instruction (classroom, lab, and clinical), and will be an integral part of the student's educational experience. The faculty member will provide engaged instruction; develop curricula; conduct program, course, and student outcomes assessment; and advise and support students. A faculty member will engage in professional work to advance the department’s mission. Average workload: 12 – 15 workload units. Duties & Responsibilities: Demonstrates knowledge and clinical expertise in teaching assigned nursing courses (clinical and didactic). Collaboratively works with faculty, students, and staff in facilities to ensure positive clinical learning experiences for student nurses. Provides student advisement, holds weekly office hours and counsels student advisees as needed. Assumes leadership roles with faculty in the development, implementation, evaluation, and revision of curriculum. Communicate with department chair and colleagues regarding student issues and progression in the program. Seeks leadership roles within the nursing program, College of Aviation, Science and Nursing, and University committees. Engages in scholarship and service to forward the discipline of Nursing. Other duties as assigned. Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Quality: Accuracy. Supports improvement and innovation in the workplace. Demonstrates awareness of and supports the nursing program and HSU operating goals through participation in quality improvement and departmental activities. Uses feedback to improve performance. Job Knowledge: Skills. Demonstrates the ability to learn. Keeps abreast of developments in their clinical nursing field, educational pedagogy, and instructional technologies. Understands how the job relates to others, the relationship of the nursing program to University committees. Uses resources efficiently. Problem Solving: Teamwork. Takes initiative to identify and solve problems. Identifies problems in a timely manner. Analyzes information and develops alternative solutions. Resolves problems early and works well in groups. Communication: Establishes and maintains open communications to enhance team effort. Presents a personal and positive model of the nursing program and HSU to students, visitors, fellow faculty and staff, and the general public. Verbal and writing ability. Good listening. Keeps others informed. Initiative: Makes a continuous effort to identify opportunities to meet/exceed customer needs and expectations. Seeks increased responsibilities. Volunteers readily. Takes individual actions and calculated risks. Asks for help when needed. Adaptability: Demonstrates flexibility in response to unexpected changes in work volume, emergencies, staffing, scheduling, and student needs. Accepts criticism and feedback. Manages competing demands. Changes approach or method to best fit situation. Judgment: Makes decisions in a timely manner. Exhibits sound, accurate judgment. Supports and explains reasons for decisions. Follows due process in student assessments and grading. Cost Consciousness: Promotes cost effectiveness through the proper use and conservation of supplies and equipment. Identifies cost-saving measures. Cooperation: Establishes effective relationships within the nursing program, Henderson State University, and the surrounding healthcare community. Looks for opportunities to assist co-workers. Works collaboratively with all HSU programs. Exhibits a positive outlook and pleasant manner. Resolves conflicts. Dependability: Fulfills work schedule and commitments. Follows instructions. Takes responsibility for own actions. Commits to doing the best job possible. Keeps students and supervisors advised of class changes. Safety: Works in a safe manner. Maintains a safe and clean work environment. Reports needed repairs or potential hazards to the appropriate department as soon as identified. Reports all on-the-job injuries and seeks medical attention as appropriate. Role models universal precautions in clinical settings. Confidentiality: Holds in trust the confidences of another. Exhibits behaviors that protect the privacy of HSU students and employees. Exhibits knowledge and compliance with HPPA when dealing with clinical issues. Corporate Compliance: Maintains awareness of, develops an understanding of, and adheres to all HSU and clinical site compliance program procedures. Is familiar with departmental, academic, and university policies and procedures; uses website and handbook to assure compliance with policies and procedures. General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Additional hours as requested and/or needed Other: Minimum Qualifications: To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily. Master of Science in Nursing (Candidates enrolled in an MSN program may be considered, completion date must be within 1 year of hire date) . Terminal nursing degree preferred . Teaching experience preferred. E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Share Apply Now"
    },
